//? Title: Quickselect: actual three-way bands and duplicate-safe median-of-medians
//? Subtitle: Actual canonical histories, retained original fixtures and explicit controls
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
An order statistic asks for one ranked key without sorting every key.
Quickselect discards the strict partition that cannot contain that rank and
stops anywhere inside the equal-pivot band. Actual native partitions replace the
old report-local counting algorithm. The original nine-key queries, ascending
fifteen-key median and seeded60-trial scaling workload remain; both pivot
strategies now handle duplicate bands directly.
)

\toc

> Mechanism and mathematical scope

A partition of \([l,h)\) produces three contiguous regions,
$$ x<p\quad|\quad x=p\quad|\quad x>p. $$
\alttext(Three-way partition separates keys below, equal to and above the selected pivot.)
The loop maintains these regions plus an unclassified suffix; a swap classifies
at least one item per iteration. If the requested absolute rank lies in the
equal region, its value is already known. Otherwise the rank remains in exactly
one strict child. This proves selection correctness by induction on shrinking
ranges, including repeated keys.

Median-of-three is deterministic and has quadratic adversarial worst cases.
BFPRT sorts groups of five, selects the median of group medians using the same
three-way producer, and discards a constant strict fraction unless an equal band
already contains the answer. Its recurrence is bounded by
\(T(n/5)+T(7n/10+O(1))+O(n)=O(n)\). A two-way equal-to-one-side partition would
invalidate that duplicate case.

> A tiny actual producing history

The table and native concept diagram read the same producing execution. Every
block below is a complete editable C++ program.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/quickselect_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    namespace a = dm::algorithms;
    namespace g = dm::graphics;
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");

    auto t = a::quickselect_trace({4, 2, 4, 1, 4, 3}, 3);
    const auto &s = t.steps[0];
    std::print("\n| actual range | pivot | equal band | actual range after partition | answer |\n| --- | " "---: | --- | --- | ---: |\n");
    for (const auto &e : t.steps)
        std::print("| [{},{}) | {} | [{},{}) | `{}` | {} |\n", e.lo, e.hi,
                   e.pivot, e.equal_begin, e.equal_end, e.values, t.value);

    g::Diagram d;
    d.node("n0", {0, 0}, std::format("Actual first pivot\n{}", s.pivot));
    d.node("n1", {10, 0},
           std::format("Actual equal rank band\n[{}, {})", s.equal_begin,
                       s.equal_end));
    d.node("n2", {20, 0}, std::format("Actual selected rank 3\n{}", t.value));
    d.edge("n0", "n1").edge("n1", "n2");
    d.save_svg("build/quickselect_tiny.svg");
}
```
