> API and interpretation

The sorted fifteen-key example is favorable to median-of-three; it is not called
adversarial here. The scaling study uses seed20240727,60 uniform trials per size
and actual comparisons including pivot selection/group sorting, rather than the
old surrogate that counted only scans. These are finite workload means, not
uncertainty intervals or a worst-case proof. BFPRT nested partition records
carry depth>0. Native ordinary signatures keep uncapped valid-input selection;
counted/trace entry points expose independently configurable work/history caps.

Reusable producers, fixtures and histories live in the canonical C++ library.
Captured records own their values and do not come from a separate report replay.
Selected counters and record/scalar policies are specified at their API
boundaries; they are not peak-byte or wall-time budgets. Synthetic structural
inputs are controlled fixtures for these mechanisms.

